    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Raised in the undeveloped suburbs of Depression-era San Diego, Gustavo Morales harbored a lifelong hatred of Asians after Japan's surrender denied him the chance to avenge his brother's death in WWII. Embraced by the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.zCWdD1NpOCn03CwE]{Gangrel} drifter Lobo Larry Vasquez, Morales patrolled the West Coast as a self-appointed guardian of wildlife refuges before settling in the Bay Area in 1978. When the Kuei-jin seized San Francisco, Morales saw his long-denied opportunity for revenge and claimed the city's parks &mdash; Golden Gate, Lincoln, the Presidio &mdash; as a personal war zone against the invaders.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Morales does his own thing regardless of what others think, and only stops when someone tougher makes him. Prince Winder tolerates his one-man war because she needs fighters like him and Mirkonen for the coming conflict, even as the Quincunx demands she call a blood hunt against him.</p>",
    "notes": "Sire: \"Lobo\" Larry Vasquez. Partner: Mirko Mirkonen. Disciplines (as printed): Animalism 2, Celerity 2, Fortitude 4, Obfuscate 2, Protean 3.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
